  message: "RUST: fixed in PR #2381 (INV-hupis satisfied, evidence on that item). The matrix row is right/right/right/unresolved/unresolved/n-a/right; its five GUESSES entries are gone from test_call_resolution_matrix.py, 20 remain in 8 languages (objc 6, groovy 5, csharp 3, javascript, php, ruby, swift, cpp, java 1 each). SIZE, first measurement on real code: on 12 Rust repositories the same-file last-writer table was behind 2,006 of 81,103 resolved Rust call edges (2.5%); at least 901 were wrong by the call's own text. No such count exists for the other eight languages. The Rust A/B scripts are in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/hupis_11242026/ (run_arm.sh, compare2.py, audit.py)."  # cdec
