  message: "OWNER RULINGS, in session 2026-11-24 (full text and plan: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/shared_resolution_design_11242026.md): build ONE shared call-resolution pass; 'unresolved beats a guess' replaces ADR-0006's 'false positives are preferable'; imports = each analyzer hands the shared pass a binding table (adopt import_scope.py, WI-tihup), the shared pass owns the lookup; a name-only match keeps its number until every edge is marked with how it was resolved, counted and sampled. Agreed order: (1) variable types per function, INV-zabud, one PR; (2) measure with no behaviour change (concept audit on 'how an edge was resolved', one mark, wider fixture WI-bobik, census); (3) the ADR (supersedes ADR-0006 scope + line 104 and ADR-0007's directory-name hints, extends ADR-0029; WI-mobih); (4) shared pieces, pilot = rust + csharp + javascript/typescript; (5) batches by mechanism, the fifteen stable-id bump items riding with the declared-name bump. The eight languages that still bind by declaration order are handled by that rollout, worst first. Import survey for the ruling: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/import_survey_11242026/RESULTS.md."  # c5db
