  message: "OWNER RULINGS, in session 2026-11-24 (late), verbatim: \"declared names for Groovy, Scala, C++ and Swift inside the next stable-id bump, or kept out of the hash. -- inside the next stable-id bump / in-place fixes for the eight guessing languages meanwhile: none, or cheap ones only -- cheap ones only / whether to cut 11.0.0 before step 4 -- no\". For this item: the eight languages that still bind by declaration order get an in-place fix ahead of the shared pass only where it is cheap (my reading of cheap: a refusal of a few lines, no new resolution machinery in the analyzer; the owner did not define the word). Which of the eight have such a fix is not known: causes are traced for Rust only. Recorded in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/shared_resolution_design_11242026.md."  # 11a8
